{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii","id":1324617,"title":"Women in Armor II","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-14T21:12:07-07:00","id":1324617,"title":"Women in Armor II","content":"A while back I started a thread in which we discussed and argued over what styles of female armor were and were not practical and appropriate. Now, I'm not going to necro a thread that ended 2 1/2 years ago, but if you want a refresher here's the link: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823821-women-in-armor-styles\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...n-armor-styles</a><br /> <br /> Well, browsing a youtube channel I just recently discovered that talks a lot about armor and weapons it seems the host also talked about a lot of what we discussed. He even adressed would women wear boobplate: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lBtvS5yhTA8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lBtvS5yhTA8</a><br /> <br /> And then did another video on the whole arguement as to if that was dangerous (spoiler, it's not, which is the opposite what a lot of forumites here thought): <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6KHz0qWQA9I&amp;t=334s\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6KHz0qWQA9I&amp;t=334s</a><br /> <br /> Just wanted to share these since Exalted is a lot about aethetics, but it seems even armor built to look cool is still practical<br /> <br /> Oh he did mention bikini armor too, bit in another context, but still interesting: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Iw_RD_h6bc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Iw_RD_h6bc</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T21:29:52-07:00","id":1324624,"title":"","content":"Ah, shad, he offers interesting insight. The bit about how a modern plate for men would resemble sensible fantasy armors more than actual antique plate (which appeals more closely to a female aesthetic) is particularly curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 07-15-2019, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T00:29:13-07:00","id":1324660,"title":"","content":"Here's another great video on the subject of sculpted armor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/1l1jpFjXv4I\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/1l1jpFjXv4I\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/1l1jpFjXv4I\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/1l1jpFjXv4I </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T01:01:40-07:00","id":1324663,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I saw a similar video that I was going to link to in the old thread, but I quit the forums for a bit because it wasn't worth the aggravation. Some people are really wedded to what they find acceptable or unacceptable in their fantasy games. *shrug*<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823821-women-in-armor-styles?p=825340#post825340\">My stance hasn't changed</a>. Exalted is an expressly magical mythic setting that says a helmet offers no protection and is purely a stylistic choice like your choice of haircut. Your armor looks however you want it to look. If you're going to run a gritty, realistic game, then more power to you but you need to nix the million things more egregious than boob plate before you convince me that hardened magical steel fitted to your body is somehow impractical. My personal preference remains for armor to be fully practical, aiconic, with as much function over form as possible (marker's marks weaken the steel). But if the person next to me wants to wear a chainmail bikini, there's nothing wrong with that.<br /> <br /> The only thing that peeves me is people who won't wear a helmet but rage-out over boob-plate being impractical. You're allowed to not like boob-plate because you think it looks silly, or you think it's sexist, or you prefer other styles, or you are afraid of boobs. Your personal preferences are valid. Embrace them. Be honest about them. Just say &quot;boob-plate makes me feel uncomfortable&quot;. Don't give me a three hour lecture about how impractical it is when your character won't even tie back their hair (<a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=_aMx50S2lv8\" target=\"_blank\">under a bear-hat or otherwise</a>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T11:44:30-07:00","id":1324781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1324663#post1324663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I saw a similar video that I was going to link to in the old thread, but I quit the forums for a bit because it wasn't worth the aggravation. Some people are really wedded to what they find acceptable or unacceptable in their fantasy games. *shrug*<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823821-women-in-armor-styles?p=825340#post825340\">My stance hasn't changed</a>. Exalted is an expressly magical mythic setting that says a helmet offers no protection and is purely a stylistic choice like your choice of haircut. Your armor looks however you want it to look. If you're going to run a gritty, realistic game, then more power to you but you need to nix the million things more egregious than boob plate before you convince me that hardened magical steel fitted to your body is somehow impractical. My personal preference remains for armor to be fully practical, aiconic, with as much function over form as possible (marker's marks weaken the steel). But if the person next to me wants to wear a chainmail bikini, there's nothing wrong with that.<br /> <br /> The only thing that peeves me is people who won't wear a helmet but rage-out over boob-plate being impractical. You're allowed to not like boob-plate because you think it looks silly, or you think it's sexist, or you prefer other styles, or you are afraid of boobs. Your personal preferences are valid. Embrace them. Be honest about them. Just say &quot;boob-plate makes me feel uncomfortable&quot;. Don't give me a three hour lecture about how impractical it is when your character won't even tie back their hair (<a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=_aMx50S2lv8\" target=\"_blank\">under a bear-hat or otherwise</a>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that when boobplate and company happens in fantasy fiction, it's not because a character chose it to be provocative, but because someone was aiming to create a sex fantasy as opposed to an action-based fantasy. Because this sort of progression has so saturated fantasy art, a lot of people are understandably very sore on the point of bikini witches and boobplate, especially when the dodge of &quot;creativity&quot; is used. Because is it actually creative if it's following in the well-beaten lockstep of hundreds of other stories posing all the women as pin-ups in lingerie?<br /> <br /> (Hint: The answer is no.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T12:39:43-07:00","id":1324794,"title":"","content":"Something else of note are the chest protection plates that are used in fencing. <a href=\"https://www.absolutefencinggear.com/shopping/product_info.php/products_id/74\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.absolutefencinggear.com/...products_id/74</a> and <a href=\"https://www.absolutefencinggear.com/shopping/product_info.php/products_id/1553/cPath/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.absolutefencinggear.com/...id/1553/cPath/</a><br /> <br /> Nothing sexualized, just there for protection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T13:20:52-07:00","id":1324798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1324781#post1324781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that when boobplate and company happens in fantasy fiction, it's not because a character chose it to be provocative, but because someone was aiming to create a sex fantasy as opposed to an action-based fantasy. Because this sort of progression has so saturated fantasy art, a lot of people are understandably very sore on the point of bikini witches and boobplate, especially when the dodge of &quot;creativity&quot; is used. Because is it actually creative if it's following in the well-beaten lockstep of hundreds of other stories posing all the women as pin-ups in lingerie?<br /> <br /> (Hint: The answer is no.)</div> </div> </div> </div>They can absolutely be sore about it, I believe JohnDoe covered that on his post. <br /> &quot;Your personal preferences are valid. Embrace them.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I happen to agree with him. Please, embrace them. They are yours, as are your reasons to have them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T14:23:30-07:00","id":1324810,"title":"","content":"I feel it goes a bit beyond personal tastes though. I find this stuff an active detriment to pretty much anything that uses it. Be it a RPG book's art piece, a comic book, whatever: when I see these designs I'm just immediately torn out of a story. They're <i>that</i> stupid looking to me.<br /> <br /> It gets annoying: a friend was talking about a kinda interesting anime, really sounded like my jam, so I start ep 1... and our lead is standing on a rooftop, in broad daylight in a lousy TNA costume. I'd heard plot synopses of this show. I knew I'd be interested. But that design was enough to get me to not check the show out any further. That's not as simple as 'it's just not for me'. The look gets a sigh and I take a brake from it <i>at best</i>, at worse this stuff makes me just abandon the work.<br /> <br /> And I don't have this reaction to scantily clad ladies in other contexts or presentations. If I know I'm watching a romcom, or a silly echi sports parody, I can roll with it, have a good time. But when these outfits are thrown into an otherwise 'straight' setting they're very immediately distancing, in a way more subtle inconsistencies like the lack of a helmet or fancified armor aren't. Those are more the things you might pick up later, rewatching a scene, thinking about it. Boob Plate is more on the obvious side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T18:15:42-07:00","id":1325808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1324810#post1324810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel it goes a bit beyond personal tastes though. I find this stuff an active detriment to pretty much anything that uses it. Be it a RPG book's art piece, a comic book, whatever: when I see these designs I'm just immediately torn out of a story. They're <i>that</i> stupid looking to me.<br /> <br /> It gets annoying: a friend was talking about a kinda interesting anime, really sounded like my jam, so I start ep 1... and our lead is standing on a rooftop, in broad daylight in a lousy TNA costume. I'd heard plot synopses of this show. I knew I'd be interested. But that design was enough to get me to not check the show out any further. That's not as simple as 'it's just not for me'. The look gets a sigh and I take a brake from it <i>at best</i>, at worse this stuff makes me just abandon the work.<br /> <br /> And I don't have this reaction to scantily clad ladies in other contexts or presentations. If I know I'm watching a romcom, or a silly echi sports parody, I can roll with it, have a good time. But when these outfits are thrown into an otherwise 'straight' setting they're very immediately distancing, in a way more subtle inconsistencies like the lack of a helmet or fancified armor aren't. Those are more the things you might pick up later, rewatching a scene, thinking about it. Boob Plate is more on the obvious side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still sounds like preference to me, just a difference in scale. Disliking something a little bit and disliking something to the point it brings you completely out of the story are both still disliking something. Disliking something in some contexts but not in others is still disliking something.<br /> There's absolutely nothing wrong with disliking something. Nothing wrong with liking something either. That's what preference is all about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25279-elowin","name":"Elowin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T00:58:28-07:00","id":1325904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elowin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1325808#post1325808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still sounds like preference to me, just a difference in scale. Disliking something a little bit and disliking something to the point it brings you completely out of the story are both still disliking something. Disliking something in some contexts but not in others is still disliking something.<br /> There's absolutely nothing wrong with disliking something. Nothing wrong with liking something either. That's what preference is all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Preference is a factor that weighs my tastes. I can watch a work that isn't to my preference and still appreciate it just fine. I prefer female leads but that doesn't mean I'll literally never watch a show with a male lead. Oversexualized costumes go beyond that, in that they're disruptive enough to make me not want to continue watching things I'd otherwise enjoy. 'This ruins the show for me' goes beyond personal preference as a matter of intensity. If you like that sorta design, hey, I ain't gonna judge you for that but I'm gonna complain about it and root for them to be gone from everything purely because that lets me enjoy more things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T04:11:09-07:00","id":1325929,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's called preference. It's cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T06:39:38-07:00","id":1325966,"title":"","content":"I don't mind a small amount of sexualised fantasy art, but there's so much that it makes it awkward for me to find non-sexualised fantasy art of women (it's easy for men). It's difficult to find good art of women in practical-looking armour; yes, I know that a lot of pictures of men in armour lacks helmets, etc, but a)maybe the helmet is on the floor off-screen, or it's been knocked off his head, and b)there's enough that some of them that you can skip past the WoW shoulder pads and find good stuff.<br /> <br /> Like I was looking for a picture to use for a cat-Lunar in our Egypt-expy game, and google images basically only showed me sexy catgirls, not the badass I wanted.<br /> <br /> It's too restrictive.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, I did find that if you're searching for pictures of samurai, as I do for my Lunar Barbarians vs DB Samurai game, googling &quot;L5R female samurai art&quot; rather than &quot;female samurai art&quot; leads to much more practical looking stuff. I mean, yes of course there's no ugly samurai girls, but the overall standard is more practical. Putting &quot;Paizo&quot; at the beginning of your google image search also helps. Just a bit of advice there.<br /> Oh, the worst is &quot;female techpriest&quot; though. &quot;Female samurai&quot; is way better than that.)<br /> <br /> I think Saur Ops Specialist has the point, essentially.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because this sort of progression has so saturated fantasy art, a lot of people are understandably very sore on the point of bikini witches and boobplate, especially when the dodge of &quot;creativity&quot; is used. Because is it actually creative if it's following in the well-beaten lockstep of hundreds of other stories posing all the women as pin-ups in lingerie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Saturated is the right word.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, his video about chainmail bikinis is poor at addressing why people feel female barbarians are objectifying, but he makes some reasonable points about the practicalities of naked fighting (and shields) and what kind of armour is and isn't useful.<br /> (I'd also mention that our image of the DnD Barbarian is talking about, well, Barbarians: ancient north and north-east Europeans, not Africans. That's very different. Vikings, Goths and Celts lived in a very cold climate! So I'm not sure pictures of Africans not wearing armour is very relevant.)<br /> <br /> I would say though, that many people when addressing the level of armour different warriors wore in history often fail to address one main reason people didn't wear a lot of armour, not just mobility or heat; but also money and technology.<br /> <br /> For the naked celtic warriors, they weren't choosing not to wear plate armour; it simply didn't exist. They didn't even have chainmail available. And most medieval soldiers wore chainmail because they couldn't afford plate armour (steel was 50x more expensive, relative to food, than it is today). When you imagine knights' plate armour, well there's a reason that was the armour of the very rich, not your average soldier, who was wearing boiled armour and chainmail, and if he had any solid steel it was his helmet.<br /> (And again, in his video clips of Africans, those are herders in very hot climates. Why would they wear armour? Most of them are not professional soldiers in a centralised state that can afford to outfit its soldiers in heavy armour anyway. Plus, he's showing pictures of modern Africans; why wear a bunch of metal armour when an angry farmer might shoot you with a gun? None of my relatives who were in the army, Royal airforce, Royal Engineers or volunteered to fight angry martial artists wore much armour either. Just a helmet.<br /> The professional armies of the Empires of Songhay and Mali however, did wear chainmail or thick leather, and they were fighting in the Sahel which is really, really hot.)<br /> <br /> So, in Exalted, most Harborheadian raiders, warriors, and even the Brides of Ahlat, don't wear a lot of armour, just shields. And that's partly heat*, partly endurance, but probably mainly because it's way too expensive for your average cattle rustler.<br /> <br /> *In the deserts of the Middle East, Mamluk, Arab, Crusader, Turkish and Persian warriors did in fact wear chainmail, but with big surcoats to keep it cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-19-2019, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T07:06:32-07:00","id":1325971,"title":"","content":"I'm...not sure you are placing those criticisms well.<br /> <br /> He's not comparing d&amp;d barbarians to their cultural inspirations because that point is moot.<br /> The question he tried to answer there is &quot;what is the more credible scenario where your wilder combatants fight mostly naked&quot;.<br /> He mentioned the african warriors because, well, they are a decent reference on how to fight unarmored. Same for the celts.<br /> The whys are secondary, where his whole point was &quot;you can make up cultural values like that&quot;, coupled with &quot;there's going to be some pratical reason behind it on some level&quot;. Heat and material availability were implied in his examples, even.<br /> <br /> So...as far as I can tell, your criticisms of his video...are in agreement to it. I suggest a reevaluation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T09:33:09-07:00","id":1326019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1325966#post1325966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind a small amount of sexualised fantasy art, but there's so much that it makes it awkward for me to find non-sexualised fantasy art of women (it's easy for men). It's difficult to find good art of women in practical-looking armour; yes, I know that a lot of pictures of men in armour lacks helmets, etc, but a)maybe the helmet is on the floor off-screen, or it's been knocked off his head, and b)there's enough that some of them that you can skip past the WoW shoulder pads and find good stuff.<br /> <br /> Like I was looking for a picture to use for a cat-Lunar in our Egypt-expy game, and google images basically only showed me sexy catgirls, not the badass I wanted.<br /> <br /> It's too restrictive.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, I did find that if you're searching for pictures of samurai, as I do for my Lunar Barbarians vs DB Samurai game, googling &quot;L5R female samurai art&quot; rather than &quot;female samurai art&quot; leads to much more practical looking stuff. I mean, yes of course there's no ugly samurai girls, but the overall standard is more practical. Putting &quot;Paizo&quot; at the beginning of your google image search also helps. Just a bit of advice there.<br /> Oh, the worst is &quot;female techpriest&quot; though. &quot;Female samurai&quot; is way better than that.)<br /> <br /> I think Saur Ops Specialist has the point, essentially.<br /> <br /> Saturated is the right word.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, his video about chainmail bikinis is poor at addressing why people feel female barbarians are objectifying, but he makes some reasonable points about the practicalities of naked fighting (and shields) and what kind of armour is and isn't useful.<br /> (I'd also mention that our image of the DnD Barbarian is talking about, well, Barbarians: ancient north and north-east Europeans, not Africans. That's very different. Vikings, Goths and Celts lived in a very cold climate! So I'm not sure pictures of Africans not wearing armour is very relevant.)<br /> <br /> I would say though, that many people when addressing the level of armour different warriors wore in history often fail to address one main reason people didn't wear a lot of armour, not just mobility or heat; but also money and technology.<br /> <br /> For the naked celtic warriors, they weren't choosing not to wear plate armour; it simply didn't exist. They didn't even have chainmail available. And most medieval soldiers wore chainmail because they couldn't afford plate armour (steel was 50x more expensive, relative to food, than it is today). When you imagine knights' plate armour, well there's a reason that was the armour of the very rich, not your average soldier, who was wearing boiled armour and chainmail, and if he had any solid steel it was his helmet.<br /> (And again, in his video clips of Africans, those are herders in very hot climates. Why would they wear armour? Most of them are not professional soldiers in a centralised state that can afford to outfit its soldiers in heavy armour anyway. Plus, he's showing pictures of modern Africans; why wear a bunch of metal armour when an angry farmer might shoot you with a gun? None of my relatives who were in the army, Royal airforce, Royal Engineers or volunteered to fight angry martial artists wore much armour either. Just a helmet.<br /> The professional armies of the Empires of Songhay and Mali however, did wear chainmail or thick leather, and they were fighting in the Sahel which is really, really hot.)<br /> <br /> So, in Exalted, most Harborheadian raiders, warriors, and even the Brides of Ahlat, don't wear a lot of armour, just shields. And that's partly heat*, partly endurance, but probably mainly because it's way too expensive for your average cattle rustler.<br /> <br /> *In the deserts of the Middle East, Mamluk, Arab, Crusader, Turkish and Persian warriors did in fact wear chainmail, but with big surcoats to keep it cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t believe you are dissing cat girls oz, shame on you. Just because they are sexy doesn\u2019t mean they aren\u2019t badass. That\u2019s sexist. Just look at Aisha Clan Clan from outlaw star.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","user":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","date":". 07-19-2019, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T13:30:19-07:00","id":1326090,"title":"","content":"Celts did have chain mail. Celts <i>invented</i> chain mail","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T13:59:15-07:00","id":1326098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326090#post1326090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celts did have chain mail. Celts <i>invented</i> chain mail</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. My current campaign is using a culture which is based on <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Orlanthi <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Celts with some Norse and Slavic touches, and they are pretty well armored. Chain mails everywhere! (for the rich, at least)</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T14:21:41-07:00","id":1326106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1325929#post1325929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's called preference. It's cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's dismissive. If an element is bad enough to leave me unable to watch a show, then while calling it a preference is technically accurate, it reduces my issue to the same level of 'I'd rather my anime characters had realistic hair rather than brightly coloured'. I don't find those two points equitable and linking the two comes off as pedantry to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1325966#post1325966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind a small amount of sexualised fantasy art, but there's so much that it makes it awkward for me to find non-sexualised fantasy art of women (it's easy for men). It's difficult to find good art of women in practical-looking armour; yes, I know that a lot of pictures of men in armour lacks helmets, etc, but a)maybe the helmet is on the floor off-screen, or it's been knocked off his head, and b)there's enough that some of them that you can skip past the WoW shoulder pads and find good stuff.<br /> <br /> Like I was looking for a picture to use for a cat-Lunar in our Egypt-expy game, and google images basically only showed me sexy catgirls, not the badass I wanted.<br /> <br /> It's too restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I just say a resounding here bloody here to this? Especially on the finding character art. Even when you strike lucky and do find something that's not gross, half the time it's got design elements that don't work, or is too recognizable. Going back to catgirls again, if pressed, I <i>can </i>think of a catgirl character who wasn't highly sexualised: Blake Belladonna from RWBY. However, her outfit <i>really</i> wouldn't work in an Egyptian styled game, and the show is popular enough that I couldn't just use art of her and expect other players to see my character. They'd just see Blake.<br /> <br /> Also yeah, it's not just 'no sex in my fantasy'. Konosuba and Okaasan are both great at balancing more sexy designs with fun stories that make them make sense. But it's bloody everywhere, and nine times out of ten it's senseless and annoying in a way too obvious to ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T14:34:07-07:00","id":1326107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326090#post1326090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celts did have chain mail. Celts <i>invented</i> chain mail</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but in the video he's talking about the Celts of north-west Europe when Rome first invaded (just because Carpathian celts made chain mail doesn't mean British ones had it, Carpathia is quite far from Britain) who apparently fought in the buff, and I think all the Roman accounts that talk about them fighting naked don't mention chain mail (some mention that a few Celts used iron breastplates, but most didn't have any armour).<br /> <br /> I don't remember them claiming that Carpathian Celts fought naked.<br /> <br /> (Of course, you should never assume that Roman accounts of barbarians are that accurate anyway, I guess)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-19-2019, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T16:02:13-07:00","id":1326120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326106#post1326106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's dismissive. If an element is bad enough to leave me unable to watch a show, then while calling it a preference is technically accurate, it reduces my issue to the same level of 'I'd rather my anime characters had realistic hair rather than brightly coloured'. I don't find those two points equitable and linking the two comes off as pedantry to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can I just say a resounding here bloody here to this? Especially on the finding character art. Even when you strike lucky and do find something that's not gross, half the time it's got design elements that don't work, or is too recognizable. Going back to catgirls again, if pressed, I <i>can </i>think of a catgirl character who wasn't highly sexualised: Blake Belladonna from RWBY. However, her outfit <i>really</i> wouldn't work in an Egyptian styled game, and the show is popular enough that I couldn't just use art of her and expect other players to see my character. They'd just see Blake.<br /> <br /> Also yeah, it's not just 'no sex in my fantasy'. Konosuba and Okaasan are both great at balancing more sexy designs with fun stories that make them make sense. But it's bloody everywhere, and nine times out of ten it's senseless and annoying in a way too obvious to ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Y'know, I'm actually starting to become curios about what the anime you mentioned at first was?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T16:28:57-07:00","id":1326123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326120#post1326120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, I'm actually starting to become curios about what the anime you mentioned at first was?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magical Girl Spec Ops Asuka. Circlet Princess had the same effect on me, but Asuka is the one my friend was talking about that I feel I'd have been down with, good or bad, bar that stupid costume. Dark magical girl stuff is the sorta thing I love to watch and talk about, whatever the quality of the work as a rule. (I had a blast watching Magical Girl Site, though I'd never claim it was good or others should check it out) Can't truthfully say C P would've been as interesting to me, for all I know it's a purely ecchi show that I started watching by mistake..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T02:06:41-07:00","id":1326219,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://www.nerfnow.com/img/1040/1654.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T02:14:36-07:00","id":1326222,"title":"","content":"As I said, the difference is that if you see a picture of an armoured woman without a helmet, maybe it's been knocked off her head, or it's on the floor, or she took it off because she couldn't see well and she'll put it back on. (Same for a man)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/76/20/22/7620226bb95a08d6da9f04845d109e01.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/76/20/22/7620226bb95a08d6da9f04845d109e01.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/76/20/22/7620226bb95a08d6da9f04845d109e01.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.pinimg.com/originals/76/20/22/7620226bb95a08d6da9f04845d109e01.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Whereas someone in a chainmail bikini is... well, when is anyone ever going to wear that? Barbarian-land is too damn cold!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T02:55:53-07:00","id":1326226,"title":"","content":"Plus no helmet is near universal in fantasy outfitting for simple dramatic reasons. It adds to a scene to be able to see a character's face and emotional reactions more clearly. Which is why you generally see them more on villains: hiding the emotional human side and making them look more intimidating.<br /> <br /> Chainmail bikinis are there for fetishization. That's it. I'll take inaccurate but useful for artistic reasons over sexualized BS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T03:21:08-07:00","id":1326231,"title":"","content":"One thing I can add as someone that draws a lot as to why at least I sometimes draw impractical equipment.<br /> Anatomy is plain and simply more fun to draw than armor.<br /> You can catch far more motion when you can see the muscles than when it's covered with armor.<br /> This doesn't mean that it's impossible to catch motion with armored characters, it's just that it's very, VERY difficult with some armors and poses (shoulder plates are evil).<br /> That's at least my reasoning.<br /> <br /> And just swift suggestion to Wizard for Egyptian catgirl, I'd suggest going for something like a black colored beerus with boobs, the species of cat alone is enough to make most people think Egypt.<br /> That will give you a pretty decent warform I'd say.<br /> Also Egypt is a pretty tricky one to design for without the character becoming sexy just due to the design of the clothes that (at least I) tend to associate with ancient Egypt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T03:39:21-07:00","id":1326233,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I'm not saying that all women (or men) in art should be armoured.<br /> <br /> Heat, price, technology, mobility, convenience (if you're, say, a guard, you don't want to wear heavy armour all day every day), weight, these are all reasons why someone might not wear armour. Things mentioned in the video, and which we've also talked about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just that, if they are wearing armour, it should be drawn to look at least somewhat practical. A bit of ornamentation on heavy armour, sure, but as he says at the end of that video (the bit I thought was the best part), a lot of the &quot;armour&quot; that fantasy art puts women in is pretty much useless; at that point, you'd be far better off having a light-ish wooden shield and wearing regular clothes for your region.<br /> <br /> I guess, to take examples from Exalted...<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/mooncalfe/art/Faka-Kun-166100292\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/mooncalfe...-Kun-166100292</a><br /> This is okay. She lives in the south (too hot for thick armour), she wants a lot of mobility to fight, and she looks pretty cool.<br /> <br /> This, on the other hand, is stupid:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/lmeFuNc.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/lmeFuNc.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgur.com/lmeFuNc.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.imgur.com/lmeFuNc.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is the artist we used to call the &quot;pantie artist&quot; because a lot of their characters are like this. Breastplate, shoulderplates, all fairly heavy stuff... and no protection at all on the crotch, just underwear with a little heart on it.<br /> This Lintha is going to get stabbed in the crotch with a daiklaive (that's not a euphamism), and it won't be pretty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And again, hey, if your fetish is chainmail bikinis you do that, but there's so damn much of it that it makes it difficult to find fantasy art of women that look tough and strong, suitable for adventurers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also Egypt is a pretty tricky one to design for without the character becoming sexy just due to the design of the clothes that (at least I) tend to associate with ancient Egypt. </div> </div> </div>A not unreasonable point, but mostly they're in sexy (and slightly uncomfortable-looking) poses rather than, say, punching a dude or slashing with a khopesh like the men generally are.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I just gave up in the end. I'm going to bring back my old Owl-dude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-20-2019, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T03:59:44-07:00","id":1326235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326233#post1326233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I'm not saying that all women (or men) in art should be armoured.<br /> <br /> Heat, price, technology, mobility, convenience (if you're, say, a guard, you don't want to wear heavy armour all day every day), weight, these are all reasons why someone might not wear armour. Things mentioned in the video, and which we've also talked about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just that, if they are wearing armour, it should be drawn to look at least somewhat practical. A bit of ornamentation on heavy armour, sure, but as he says at the end of that video (the bit I thought was the best part), a lot of the &quot;armour&quot; that fantasy art puts women in is pretty much useless; at that point, you'd be far better off having a light-ish wooden shield and wearing regular clothes for your region.<br /> <br /> And again, hey, if your fetish is chainmail bikinis you do that, but there's so damn much of it that it makes it difficult to find fantasy art of women that look tough and strong, suitable for adventurers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, kinda wish that google would allow us to filter things a bit easier, cause trust me. I know your pain about trying to find the proper armor and instead get red Sonjas a plenty or those god forsaken shoulder pads of killing all joy in drawing armor...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326233#post1326233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A not unreasonable point, but mostly they're in sexy (and slightly uncomfortable-looking) poses rather than, say, punching a dude or slashing with a khopesh like the men generally are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmm this is true...<br /> Heck, you actually rarely see any grizzled warrior women in media.<br /> And when you find them they tend to have the &quot;Borderline Psychopath&quot; personality...<br /> Or now that I think about it... There's one tough as nails woman that's a fighter that I can think of that doesn't go all blushy or is a irredeemable psychopath or anything like that and just remains a tough, hard as nails badass would be the dwarf Gnolga from the series Gold Digger.<br /> Sure, there's fanservice in that comic and quite a bit of it but never of Gnolga (at least from my memory).<br /> <br /> But now I'm ranting so I'll stop doing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T08:51:03-07:00","id":1326278,"title":"","content":"I had to spent a lot of time in Pinterest to filter out the bikini chainmails and get the kind of badass characters I want in my stories, but now I'm glad I did. There's a lot of great non-pandering art out there, but it definitely takes more time and effort to find it compared to the fanservice.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> may this heal your ailing heart <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/b58f8381a87b96be58591c3f038d8a16/tumblr_pa1h86miFA1si41yfo1_1280.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/b58f8381a87b96be58591c3f038d8a16/tumblr_pa1h86miFA1si41yfo1_1280.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/b58f8381a87b96be58591c3f038d8a16/tumblr_pa1h86miFA1si41yfo1_1280.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://66.media.tumblr.com/b58f8381a87b96be58591c3f038d8a16/tumblr_pa1h86miFA1si41yfo1_1280.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T09:41:07-07:00","id":1326290,"title":"","content":"That's good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T20:23:46-07:00","id":1326394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326090#post1326090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celts did have chain mail. Celts <i>invented</i> chain mail</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;The earliest examples of surviving mail were found in the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carpathian_Basin\" target=\"_blank\">Carpathian Basin</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> at a burial in Horn\u00fd Jatov, Slovakia dated at 3rd century BC, and in a chieftain's burial located in </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ciume%C8%99ti\" target=\"_blank\">Ciume\u0219ti</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romania\" target=\"_blank\">Romania</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">.</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chain_mail#cite_note-urlCeltic_Chainmail_|_Brendan_Mac_Gonagle_-_Academia.edu-3\" target=\"_blank\">[3]</a></sup><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chain_mail#cite_note-urlCeltic_chainmail_%E2%80%93_Balkan_Celts-4\" target=\"_blank\">[4]</a></sup><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chain_mail#cite_note-5\" target=\"_blank\">[5]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Its invention is commonly credited to the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celts\" target=\"_blank\">Celts</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">,</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chain_mail#cite_note-books.google.com-6\" target=\"_blank\">[6]</a></sup><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> but there are examples of </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etruscan_military_history\" target=\"_blank\">Etruscan</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> pattern mail dating from at least the 4th century BCE.&quot; Wiki says no. </span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T00:17:45-07:00","id":1326410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326394#post1326394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&amp;quot;The earliest examples of surviving mail were found in the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carpathian_Basin&amp;quot;]Carpathian</a> Basin[/URL]<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> at a burial in Horn\u00fd Jatov, Slovakia dated at 3rd century BC, and in a chieftain's burial located in </span></span></span><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ciume%C8%99ti&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Ciume\u0219ti</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, </span></span></span><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romania&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Romania</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">.</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chain_mail#cite_note-urlCeltic_Chainmail_|_Brendan_Mac_Gonagle_-_Academia.edu-3&amp;quot;]</a>[3][/URL]</sup><sup><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chain_mail#cite_note-urlCeltic_chainmail_%E2%80%93_Balkan_Celts-4&amp;quot;]</a>[4][/URL]</sup><sup><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chain_mail#cite_note-5&amp;quot;]</a>[5][/URL]</sup><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Its invention is commonly credited to the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celts&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Celts</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">,</span></span></span><sup><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chain_mail#cite_note-books.google.com-6&amp;quot;]</a>[6][/URL]</sup><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> but there are examples of </span></span></span><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etruscan_military_history&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Etruscan</a><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> pattern mail dating from at least the 4th century BCE.&amp;quot; Wiki says no. </span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Etruscans used ringed lamella. That's not chain mail. The three cited referrences seem to refer to Japanese lamella. But I'm open to a secondary source here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T20:15:13-07:00","id":1326590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326410#post1326410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Etruscans used ringed lamella. That's not chain mail. The three cited referrences seem to refer to Japanese lamella. But I'm open to a secondary source here.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a certain irony in saying &quot;I don't trust your sources which neither of us have on hand. Here's an unsourced claim that backs me up. But I'm willing to let you find more sources&quot;. Whelp, who knows. Maybe Gilgamesh invented chainmail in 10000 BC when he killed the Bull of Heaven. <br /> <br /> Anyway. I'm going to go against the grain and declare my unironic, totally sincere love for silly impractical sexy armor. I love that Volfer fights in a speedo and the arm part of a set of super heavy plate. I love that he battles with a metal surfboard while deflecting blades off his rockhard abs. I love &quot;boobplates&quot;. I remember Her Redness and the &quot;thighgate&quot; conspiracy. Clothes, cloaks, revealed stomachs, silly over the top spiky bad guy death armor? All of it. I love all of it. I don't care if that means I lose the 2019 Forum award for Most Woke Bloke. <br /> <br /> If anyone needs me I'm gonna be on pinterest finding fantasy women warriors in kickass poses in revealing armor. Because I'm a terrible horrible no good very bad person. .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T07:06:18-07:00","id":1326690,"title":"","content":"The Shadiversity YouTube channel is really good! Shad is a lovable nerd, clearly very knowledgeable, and while he goes on about &quot;historical accuracy&quot; a bit more than I personally care for, I think he manages to walk the line of pointing out unrealistic fantasy tropes without adding an implied &quot;...and that's terrible!&quot; at the end. I got into his channel from the video about <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0EWi2DnDoaI\" target=\"_blank\">wearing swords on your back</a>, and he recently made a video about how <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0zBsUdUKmhk\" target=\"_blank\">magical materials might influence weapon design</a>, which I think might be interesting for this forum.<br /> <br /> Now, regarding the famous bikini witches, I've stated my opinions on these kinds of things previously. I <i>think</i> most of them are consistent, although I'm sure they've changed more than I realise. The core of my stance is that presentation and representation of women is a structural phenomenon, which includes all the instances of such representation, the contexts they're presented in, and the impacts they might have on society.<br /> <br /> To put it simply: I personally think it's okay to like bikini barbarians. I think, in fact, that Exalted provides a context that supports them. Exalted has silken armour that looks like normal silk clothes but is strong as steel, and Resistance Charms that greatly reduce the need for armour at all. Anyone playing such characters at their table, meaning a place with very limited social impact, can only be held accountable by those exposed to it, that is, essentially those participating in the same game.<br /> <br /> It's important to note that Exalted also provides a context that supports heavily armoured female knights. Magical materials and some other Resistance Charms provide great benefit to wearing a big hulking cage of metal around you, to greatly reduced downsides. The same as above goes for those.<br /> <br /> Because both of these aesthetics (in a generalised sense, of course most cases are somewhere in between) are supported, I think the game should present both of them visually. Perfect Soul is as supported by the game as The Lady of Darkness in Bloodstained Robes is, and that should show. However, since the state of fantasy art is as it is, it is probably more important for the game publications to emphasise the armoured side of the spectrum, if nothing else then because there are more ways to be dressed than to be naked.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I think the game should support different states of dress and undress of male characters. Jace and Volfer, again, are both quite supported aesthetics.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's much more to this discussion. Right now, we've only talked about states of armouredness. Presentation and representation of characters go much deeper than that, and I personally think Exalted does pretty well with providing a point of variety in the fantasy genre in terms of societal gender norms and empowerment. Really, if I could rant a bit, Exalted art seems like some of the least in need of pinup aesthetics when one of the historically most attractive attributes has been power. The blowup that happened around Sublime Danger (That's what, 4 years ago now? Time flies.) focused so much on her clothes and body shape, and here I was wondering if no one noticed how freaking hot it was that she was <i>levitating twenty swords</i>. Likewise, the Scarlet Empress is one of my favourite characters in the game, and very little of that is due to what she looks like.<br /> <br /> A way for the game to go is a further contextualisation of nudity and sexuality. If we can show a half-naked person on top of a heap of slaughtered enemies, why can we not show them atop a heap of conquered lovers? If they're going to be naked in battle, then they can be naked otherwise as well, and it wouldn't even have to be justified with magic that time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 07-22-2019, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T09:08:43-07:00","id":1326722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326590#post1326590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a certain irony in saying &quot;I don't trust your sources which neither of us have on hand. Here's an unsourced claim that backs me up. But I'm willing to let you find more sources&quot;. Whelp, who knows. Maybe Gilgamesh invented chainmail in 10000 BC when he killed the Bull of Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not aiming to convince you but you're saying Italians invented chain mail and giving three references:<br /> <br /> Oriental Armour, H. Russell Robinson, 1967 Walker and Co., New York, pp. 11-12<br /> Catalogue of the Exhibition of Ancient Helmets and Examples of Mail, William Burgess &amp; Baron De Cosson<br /> Stone, G.C. (1934): A Glossary of the Construction, Decoration and Use of Arms And Armor in All Countries and in All Times, Dover Publications, New York<br /> <br /> I'm not convinced that a book called &quot;Oriental armor&quot; has much to do with Tuscony.<br /> <br /> Except, the most famed oriental armor is lamellar. In fact the wiki page for Lamellar armour has a section entitled <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamellar_armour\" target=\"_blank\">Japanese lamellar armour</a>.<br /> <br /> If you do a search for Etruscan Armor, you get <a href=\"http://www.ancient-battles.com/warriors/Etruscan.php\" target=\"_blank\">results</a> saying they used lamellar armor which was similiar in construction to Japanese armor. That's not conclusive proof that the Etruscans invented chain mail.<br /> <br /> The only other link in that article is the link to the wikipedia page for <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etruscan_military_history\" target=\"_blank\">Etruscan military history</a> (and you actually included it in your post) which describes Etruscan armour as being made of solid plates of bronze, not chain mail. In fact chain mail is never mentioned once on the links you provided.<br /> <br /> And, again, purely on the references that you have provided we have a website about <a href=\"https://www.routledgehandbooks.com/doi/10.4324/9780203526965.ch39#!\" target=\"_blank\">Etruscan armour</a> and it doesn't look like chain mail to me.<br /> <br /> Now wikipedia gets a lot of flakk for not being a reliable source, but the reason I didn't provide links is because your own sources directly contradict your claim. I don't think it's particularly egregious to dismiss without evidence that which is presented without evidence.<br /> <br /> The other reason I didn't post sources was because I didn't have any. I had a half-remembering from twenty years ago when I was studying history. I don't know who invented chain mail. I can't prove the Etruscan's used lamellar. But if you'd like some sources on their armour then here they are:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.truefork.org/Photography/Etruscan_Armour.php\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.truefork.org/Etruscan_files/etrusc29.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.truefork.org/Photography/Etruscan_Armour.php\" target=\"_blank\"> Arms and Armour of the Etruscans </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.truefork.org/Photography/Etruscan_Armour.php\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.truefork.org/Photography/Etruscan_Armour.php </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.ancient-battles.com/warriors/Etruscan.php\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ancient-battles.com/warriors/Etruscan.php\" target=\"_blank\"> ancient-battles.com&nbsp;-&nbsp;ancient battles Resources and Information. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ancient-battles.com/warriors/Etruscan.php\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.ancient-battles.com/warriors/Etruscan.php </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> ancient-battles.com is your first and best source for all of the information you&rsquo;re looking for. From general topics to more of what you would expect to find here, ancient-battles.com has it all. We hope you find what you are searching for! </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/Etruscan_Warfare/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.worldhistory.org/img/c/p/1200x627/6356.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/Etruscan_Warfare/\" target=\"_blank\"> Etruscan Warfare </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ancient.eu/Etruscan_Warfare/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.ancient.eu/Etruscan_Warfare/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Etruscan civilization, which flourished in central Italy from the 8th to 3rd century BCE, gained a reputation in antiquity for being party-loving pushovers when it came to warfare, but the reality... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But, again, I don't have a dog in this fight. If you've got better references I'm happy to change my opinion. Who invented chain mail really has no bearing on this discussion and isn't particularly important to my life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326590#post1326590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway. I'm going to go against the grain and declare my unironic, totally sincere love for silly impractical sexy armor. I love that Volfer fights in a speedo and the arm part of a set of super heavy plate. I love that he battles with a metal surfboard while deflecting blades off his rockhard abs. I love &quot;boobplates&quot;. I remember Her Redness and the &quot;thighgate&quot; conspiracy. Clothes, cloaks, revealed stomachs, silly over the top spiky bad guy death armor? All of it. I love all of it. I don't care if that means I lose the 2019 Forum award for Most Woke Bloke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that'd also be a preference. Well done for owning it. It is just as valid as not liking sexy armor. I hope you have fun.<br /> <br /> It's not to my personal taste in armor, but I see your point of view and I'm a big fan of things which are sexy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-23-2019, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T11:09:15-07:00","id":1326759,"title":"","content":"Context is really important.<br /> I have a live and let live approach to how people want their characters to look but I'm critical of how professional products sell themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T11:20:24-07:00","id":1326760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326590#post1326590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway. I'm going to go against the grain and declare my unironic, totally sincere love for silly impractical sexy armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a certain irony in knowing that this presentation is in the majority and declaring that you're going &quot;against the grain&quot; by liking it. Perhaps against the forum's grain, perhaps, but certainly not decades worth of fantasy art posed and dressed as pin-ups, to be sure. Hell, this thread isn't exactly short of defenders of sexy &quot;armor&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I love that Volfer fights in a speedo and the arm part of a set of super heavy plate. I love that he battles with a metal surfboard while deflecting blades off his rockhard abs. I love &quot;boobplates&quot;. I remember Her Redness and the &quot;thighgate&quot; conspiracy. Clothes, cloaks, revealed stomachs, silly over the top spiky bad guy death armor? All of it. I love all of it. I don't care if that means I lose the 2019 Forum award for Most Woke Bloke. </div> </div> </div>Not all of those are equivalent in over the top. Being covered in spikes and plates can hardly be said to be sexualizing a character, nor is Volfer's typical presentation strictly doing this, since a lot of Volfer is still in power fantasy territory. You'd need to go to the &quot;Prince Diamond: A Fanfiction&quot; to see something closer to sexualization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anyone needs me I'm gonna be on pinterest finding fantasy women warriors in kickass poses in revealing armor. Because I'm a terrible horrible no good very bad person. . </div> </div> </div>I spend notable amounts of time looking at images on Danbooru and company, and also have more than one sketchbook full of salacious drawings. I don't see that as a call to be set on sexualized character designs at every turn, nor to declare loudly in opposition to people suggesting that perhaps that sort of character design is overused and needs some off time to alternate works and maybe get full coverage fantasy art on more even footing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T11:26:55-07:00","id":1326761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326760#post1326760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a certain irony in knowing that this presentation is in the majority and declaring that you're going &quot;against the grain&quot; by liking it. Perhaps against the forum's grain, perhaps, but certainly not decades worth of fantasy art posed and dressed as pin-ups, to be sure. Hell, this thread isn't exactly short of defenders of sexy &quot;armor&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it <i>is</i> against the grain here, as people make a visible effort in pointing this out that you don't see as much with other media biases.<br /> <br /> Can't just live and let live, you know?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T12:01:57-07:00","id":1326767,"title":"","content":"I think I would agree that the stress is that a lot of it is really about balance. You can take characters like this in small doses as part of the array of characters being presented. <br /> <br /> And actually I would argue rather strongly that in small doses having characters like this present is fun, and more than that it is also enhancing to the game's feel that it is referencing the genres where character designs like this are present, and for this latter reason it is almost essential that to some degree these characters are present. For an example that exists in game already, Volfer (who Sorcerous Overlord references) is basically VanfromVisionOfEscaflowneXJechtfromFFX in character design, and that reference helps sell that Exalted is an anime-action game built on those sort of sources, and it is similar for not heavily clothed female characters who also callback reference like this in their character design. <br /> <br /> And Exalted offers a mechanical reason why characters like this would be able to function without dying laughably, which is great.<br /> <br /> But at the same time you want to avoid the feeling that every female character present is like the roster of Dead or Alive or some ridiculous harem anime, because that will be alienating and not inclusive and not fun.<br /> <br /> On female character depiction in Exalted, and in pop culture generally, these days it seems a bit of a shame that it seems at times bit polarized between the ideas that all female characters must be deliberately desexualized to strike a political and social blow against The Male Gaze (voluminous, shape concealing, &quot;modest&quot; clothes and armour, not particularly attractive silhouettes, etc), with claims that various social ills are directly attributed to the failure to do this, and on the other hand rather entitled fellows who get very irate at any suggestion that anything happen other than same few physically idealized and scantily clad sexualized waifus are presented again and again. <br /> <br /> While in reality the majority are probably exhausted with all this and see no problem with the occasional quite sexualized female character as adding a bit of fun... but would mostly prefer generally to see a nice mid range of female characters who are generally reasonably athletic and fit and obviously would be sexually attractive, without having enormous unrealistically enhanced secondary sex characteristics, wear normal, close fitting clothing without boob windows, thigh highs, etc. And that these characters have strong values and personalities and goals without unnecessary hyping them up as The Strongest, etc. Anyway, that's just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T21:52:25-07:00","id":1326878,"title":"","content":"Nice to see some new ground being broken.<br /> <br /> Somebody brought up helms earlier, and it's having me wonder if a majority of battle helms throughout history have not in fact left the face uncovered to greater or lesser extent.<br /> <br /> The fully enclosed helm seems a bit of a historical outlier to my recollection, and I'm curious about why that might be. Metalworking, tactics, or just the style at the time? Still, there are options that reconcile head protection with a visible face. Give Karal Linwei a damn kabuto, at least.<br /> <br /> Then give her a mask covering the rest of her face anyway, because those looked pretty interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T01:54:09-07:00","id":1326915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326878#post1326878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice to see some new ground being broken.<br /> <br /> Somebody brought up helms earlier, and it's having me wonder if a majority of battle helms throughout history have not in fact left the face uncovered to greater or lesser extent.<br /> <br /> The fully enclosed helm seems a bit of a historical outlier to my recollection, and I'm curious about why that might be. Metalworking, tactics, or just the style at the time? Still, there are options that reconcile head protection with a visible face. Give Karal Linwei a damn kabuto, at least.<br /> <br /> Then give her a mask covering the rest of her face anyway, because those looked pretty interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is that it was to make sure that the wearer could have as much visibility as possible combined with protection and ease of breathing.<br /> For example the roman helmet had a pretty damn good combination of everything. Extra armor on the forehead to protect from overhead swings, cheek protectors by the ears to defend against side strikes, whilst at the same time you will have nothing blocking your nose, ears, eyes or mouth giving you full access to both breathing and your senses so you can hear the orders shouted by the centurions and also see anything coming at you.<br /> This also left the helmet relatively cheap to construct as well and made it easy to repair as at least the cheek protectors where separate bits attached to the helmet meaning that if it was damaged you could easily replace that part.<br /> <br /> As for fully enclosed helmets, well I'd say it was probably just due to how expensive they became to make as you need to custom make them for every knight.<br /> Not to mention that you need to send the entire thing in for repair if there's damage dealt to it and it hindered breathing and blocked hearing, sight and muffled your voice.<br /> It did however provide some pretty darn solid defense.<br /> A good example of enclosed helmet would be the frog-mouth helmet.<br /> This was primarily a tournament helmet as it was riveted onto your chest armor, but this made you almost invulnerable to any sort of damage to the head at the cost of vision and hearing.<br /> You could literally take a tourney lance to the throat and land on your head from horseback with only a few bruises.<br /> <br /> The more standard bascinet was a simple but solid design that could be modified with visors of different shapes and sizes giving you even more protection.<br /> The benefit of having visor protection was that you could just flip up the visor if you needed to survey your surroundings or take a unobstructed breather.<br /> The visor also had the benefit of being detachable so if it or the helmet was damaged you could just replace the damaged part.<br /> The Bascinet was also a single shape and thus far more solid than the great helmet that was five different parts riveted together.<br /> <br /> Another thing that can be worth to think about is the fact that the head is not the most difficult part to hit, the actual face is far harder to hit since the opponent needs to do very little to avoid attacks aimed at the face and it's a relatively small area to hit.<br /> <br /> War masks served a similar purpose to visors, they did however tend to be designed or decorated in ways to either intentionally or just by a fluke, intimidate and demoralize the enemy.<br /> Facing an enemy whose face you cannot see can also be quite intimidating in the same way as someone showing no emotion in the face of danger can also be quite intimidating.<br /> It can also be demoralizing to face the &quot;same&quot; enemy again and again.<br /> <br /> But yeah, to summarize.<br /> When you design a helmet you usually want a good combination between protection, hearing, breathing and vision whilst also keeping it affordable.<br /> <br /> Hopefully I made some sense and didn't just ramble on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T03:54:02-07:00","id":1326924,"title":"","content":"There <i>was</i> something kind of new that bugged me, what was it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326233#post1326233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/mooncalfe/art/Faka-Kun-166100292\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/mooncalfe...-Kun-166100292</a><br /> This is okay. She lives in the south (too hot for thick armour), she wants a lot of mobility to fight, and she looks pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, this.<br /> <br /> Okay, so setting aside the fallacy of armour as something that lacks mobility...<br /> <br /> First off, the statement about it being in the South is fair enough as not wearing a particular variety of armour goes, but it would be silly to say that goes for all possible forms of armour, including tightly woven cloth, and it still doesn't fully resolve... that. People who inhabit desert regions might still wear robes or tunics, and if we were taking the idea that Faka Kun's appearance being due to patches that lack pigmentation seriously, there would also be an idea of her having grown up with an impulse to wear coverings that would prevent her from burning.<br /> <br /> But those are things that can be kind of set aside with cultural specificity and an idea that one's practices might change with the increased resilience of being Exalted.<br /> <br /> Mobility, though? Mobility is not a look that is conveyed by an outfit that is alternately tight and loose in a manner that makes it look as though the wrong move in one direction will have it slip off of you (maybe tangling a bit around your limbs), and if you move in the other it will tighten up really badly at your crotch or neck.<br /> <br /> I don't believe that I've ever seen a person who engages in an endeavour dependent on mobility dress anything like Faka Kun does.<br /> <br /> And to be honest, Faka Kun's design has always made me a bit uncomfortable because it's not just sexualised, but sexualised in a manner very reminiscent of many of the ways in which Western people have generally sexualised depictions of women indigenous to the places that they have colonised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also Egypt is a pretty tricky one to design for without the character becoming sexy just due to the design of the clothes that (at least I) tend to associate with ancient Egypt.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Being topless isn't inherently sexual, and it should be possible to convey that by a framing in which a character is treating it as entirely normal, going about regular daily business, and the uncovered breasts are not particularly glamourized. </span></span></span></div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T06:02:40-07:00","id":1326943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326924#post1326924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being topless isn't inherently sexual, and it should be possible to convey that by a framing in which a character is treating it as entirely normal, going about regular daily business, and the uncovered breasts are not particularly glamourized.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing is that I was primarily talking about their dresses.<br /> They tend to accentuate the female shape which gives her a relatively &quot;clear&quot; feminin silhouette in almost any pose.<br /> <br /> Actually, for the the topless variant the simplest thing to do to get attention away from the chest would be to make sure that the bottom part of her clothes are white and always have them close to the center of the picture since we tend to focus on bright colors...<br /> That can however lead to different problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T07:43:30-07:00","id":1326961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326924#post1326924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There <i>was</i> something kind of new that bugged me, what was it...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Right, this.<br /> <br /> Okay, so setting aside the fallacy of armour as something that lacks mobility...<br /> <br /> First off, the statement about it being in the South is fair enough as not wearing a particular variety of armour goes, but it would be silly to say that goes for all possible forms of armour, including tightly woven cloth, and it still doesn't fully resolve... that. People who inhabit desert regions might still wear robes or tunics, and if we were taking the idea that Faka Kun's appearance being due to patches that lack pigmentation seriously, there would also be an idea of her having grown up with an impulse to wear coverings that would prevent her from burning.<br /> <br /> But those are things that can be kind of set aside with cultural specificity and an idea that one's practices might change with the increased resilience of being Exalted.<br /> <br /> Mobility, though? Mobility is not a look that is conveyed by an outfit that is alternately tight and loose in a manner that makes it look as though the wrong move in one direction will have it slip off of you (maybe tangling a bit around your limbs), and if you move in the other it will tighten up really badly at your crotch or neck.<br /> <br /> I don't believe that I've ever seen a person who engages in an endeavour dependent on mobility dress anything like Faka Kun does.<br /> <br /> And to be honest, Faka Kun's design has always made me a bit uncomfortable because it's not just sexualised, but sexualised in a manner very reminiscent of many of the ways in which Western people have generally sexualised depictions of women indigenous to the places that they have colonised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not getting bogged down in a debate about this, so please feel free to reply but I'm unlikely to respond.<br /> <br /> Faka is an acrobat. She's a circus performer who wears a flowing costume. She's also a(n escaped) slave.<br /> <br /> Her costume was picked to enhance her role as a performer by her master. And culturally it's the clothing she's grown up wearing.<br /> <br /> It's not tight around the joints. It's lightweight. That's mobility.<br /> <br /> It's loose because she's also a sneak thief who needs to distract guards and squirrel items away. Plus, you know, a slave performer.<br /> <br /> Looking at the size of the head hole (which is pretty consistent) it's never going to tighten up at the neck. The crotch design seems to depend on who's drawing it, but even if it does wedgie her it's not inhibiting hip movement. Between the rings which hold the garment together and, you know, her neck it seems pretty clear that it's not going to slip off her. It might slip off a breast, but again that's kinda the point of the outfit.<br /> <br /> As for the colonisation... she was enslaved by a snakeman (a pretty unsubtle indictment against colonizing slave holders), ripped from her home and paraded around in a circus. She wears exactly what I'd expect her to wear. Now she's freed herself, freed the other slaves, stolen from the snake who enslaved her and wanders the South on a mission to lead more slaves to freedom. She could dress however she wants but she chooses to dress like this because it gets the job done and it's what she's used to. Your character can wear desert dress and admonish her for looking the way she does if you like in play: hit an intimacy and roll above her Resolve of 8 and you can even convince her to wear something else if you don't like her choices that much. I'd &quot;get&quot; your complaint if she was written as a nun but dressed in a sexualised &quot;exotic&quot; manner as this would be clearly incongruous with the character and blatant fetishism. But saying someone who's been enslaved by racists shouldn't be dressed like someone enslaved by racists strikes me as an attempt to censor creativity and sanatize Exalted into a PG13 setting where sex doesn't exist and bad things never happen. I'm sure you don't see it that way but given the great diversity in Exalted characters and the vast agency Faka shows (especially as the signature Djala), I don't see us possibly reaching an agreement on this.<br /> <br /> To me the presentation is simple. The Djala exist as a race of sex slaves, but the only Djala the Exalted line is willing to devote word count to is the hero freeing her people from slavery, kicking butt, getting rich and doing her own thing. To reduce that to &quot;this non-caucasian woman is sexualised&quot; spectacularly misses the wider social context of the character and what it is she represents and who the character speaks to, in my opinion. <br /> <br /> But you are entitled to your own opinion. My preferences are not your preferences. And if you think Faka would be better served by a jilbaab then there's nothing wrong with that -- I just don't agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-23-2019, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T14:15:31-07:00","id":1327065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326943#post1326943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny thing is that I was primarily talking about their dresses.<br /> They tend to accentuate the female shape which gives her a relatively &amp;quot;clear&amp;quot; feminin silhouette in almost any pose.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how they look in stylised pictures. Archaeology and understanding of the available materials illustrate that they'd actually be more baggy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, for the the topless variant the simplest thing to do to get attention away from the chest would be to make sure that the bottom part of her clothes are white and always have them close to the center of the picture since we tend to focus on bright colors...<br /> That can however lead to different problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Treating it as something to conceal doesn't really jibe with it being something mundane and nonsexual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T23:58:08-07:00","id":1327145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327065#post1327065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how they look in stylised pictures. Archaeology and understanding of the available materials illustrate that they'd actually be more baggy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The historical Buddha in Theravada art is a pretty good example of the difference between attire in stylized art vs how they look in real-life. And I think it kinda fits for your second point too since the Buddha and Bodhisattva regularly show their <a href=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-olsXpashbZQ/UFh0ELy_-jI/AAAAAAAABqo/-k4RcavrmVg/s1600/%25E3%2582%25B9%25E3%2582%25AD%25E3%2583%25A3%25E3%2583%25B30016.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">bare</a> <a href=\"http://livedoor.blogimg.jp/zwiebeln/imgs/7/8/785fff37.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">chest</a>, they don't hide it since they don't perceive it as sexual.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/488381373988732939/603476476381102080/Buddha_.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 07-24-2019, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T03:23:33-07:00","id":1327152,"title":"","content":"Armor being realistic is only a secondary to this particular discussion. The difference between a female protagonist being dressed and acting sexy and the barely disguised sex-doll drawn to appease the male gaze is the main point.<br /> <br /> Not saying the latter is an abomination and you should feel bad for even looking at it, let alone enjoy it, but I'd rather have the former make up the bulk of art in an RPG (or comic, or computer game, etc...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T04:05:58-07:00","id":1327156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327152#post1327152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Armor being realistic is only a secondary to this particular discussion. The difference between a female protagonist being dressed and acting sexy and the barely disguised sex-doll drawn to appease the male gaze is the main point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which was not my intention and now I feel bad for causing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T06:42:54-07:00","id":1327176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1326759#post1326759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Context is really important.<br /> I have a live and let live approach to how people want their characters to look but I'm critical of how professional products sell themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is pretty reasonable.<br /> <br /> Not exactly the same time, but one of my Lunar players wants to (in another game that I don't run/play) make a whole bunch of sexy catgirl generals to serve his (slightly pervy) sorcerer. Bit weird. But not a huge deal.<br /> <br /> Similarly, one of the PCs in the Egypt-expy game I play is an Appearance 8 foxgirl who's (officially) the Prince's concubine, and generally doesn't wear much. In 2nd ed, she had Appearance specialties in &quot;Sexy&quot; and &quot;While naked&quot;. Not a character I'd want to play, but not a big deal.<br /> <br /> But if &quot;you can make sexy catgirls!&quot; was one of the example workings in the Core book, and &quot;sexy half-naked foxgirl concubine&quot; was the signature Lunar character, I'd probably have a much more negative reaction. Stuff in books is more direction-setting for the game as a whole.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and on helmets (a discussion I missed the first time), I was going to reply but I saw Xanroth made a good reply. Visibility, breathing, the difficulty of making it, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T19:41:33-07:00","id":1327337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327176#post1327176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if &quot;you can make sexy catgirls!&quot; was one of the example workings in the Core book, and &quot;sexy half-naked foxgirl concubine&quot; was the signature Lunar character, I'd probably have a much more negative reaction. Stuff in books is more direction-setting for the game as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>This begs the question, however, of what is &quot;sensible&quot; sexual content in the book, since the game acknowledges it exists. A gag scenario like the catgirl generals is easy to write off, but<br /> 1) should it?<br /> 2) What should and shouldn't be cool to add?<br /> 3) Did the criteria move over time? Overton's a bitch.<br /> <br /> And I believe these are rather tricky questions to answer for any given time, because unsatisfied people will be louder than satisfied people pretty much by definition. How do you measure how representative of your public those people are, especially before any misjudgement starts costing you your public?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T03:42:27-07:00","id":1327379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327337#post1327337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This begs the question, however, of what is &amp;quot;sensible&amp;quot; sexual content in the book, since the game acknowledges it exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manufacturing humans for the express purpose of being objectified at best (leaving aside questions of a sufficiently different cultural background that it begs the question of what their impulse and standards for objectification are) is something a sorcerer might have conceivably done, but it's not the most pleasant thing to read about, and I wouldn't care for it being tossed in casually.<br /> <br /> I mean, presumably workings can be used to do a number of unpleasant things directly to people, but the examples overall seem to avoid that direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) What should and shouldn't be cool to add?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things that might feel unduly unwelcoming to people who don't deserve it, for a start.<br /> <br /> The issue I would see is when it talks about <u>making</u> sexy people, especially when they're all women.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Did the criteria move over time? Overton's a bitch.</div> </div> </div> </div>The world getting gradually better over time is not an insidious plot to catch people out, though.<br /> <br /> A person who is actually serious about the value of better social attitudes involved in representation is not somebody who should be upset by the notion that people in the future may see their attitudes and art as being quaint at best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I believe these are rather tricky questions to answer for any given time, because unsatisfied people will be louder than satisfied people pretty much by definition. How do you measure how representative of your public those people are, especially before any misjudgement starts costing you your public?</div> </div> </div> </div>Minority voices in one's public deserve to be listened to when they bring up topics concerned with harmful language or representation.<br /> <br /> This should not harm one's majority audience, and of it does, one should question of that's an audience one should want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T03:47:27-07:00","id":1327380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327337#post1327337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This begs the question, however, of what is &quot;sensible&quot; sexual content in the book, since the game acknowledges it exists. A gag scenario like the catgirl generals is easy to write off, but<br /> 1) should it?<br /> 2) What should and shouldn't be cool to add?<br /> 3) Did the criteria move over time? Overton's a bitch.<br /> <br /> And I believe these are rather tricky questions to answer for any given time, because unsatisfied people will be louder than satisfied people pretty much by definition. How do you measure how representative of your public those people are, especially before any misjudgement starts costing you your public?</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. There's a difference between sexual, sexy and sexualized. The first two are usually ok, the last is a great deal trickier. Taking your expected target audience into account, and the purpose of your art, seems to be key here. What flies in a porn magazine aimed at straight men obviously does not in Teen Vogue. Context matters, fancy that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, sexiness without objectification is not some hypothetical or abstract concept. Let me assure you us women enjoy looking at and playing sexy characters as much as men (if not more, but that is different question). Sex also sells to us. Really, it does. That said, and coming back to tabletop rpg's, if you want me to flip through your book and be inspired and fired up to make a character, good artwork for that would be a woman who is sexy as well as looks as if she has agency, motivation, personality, dignity and autonomy. You know, just like the male characters are supposed to be. The usual vacant-eyed, slack-jawed floozy, impossibly bent so both her breasts and ass are prominently visible, passively doing nothing, yeah, no, does nothing except making me wonder if I'm even the target audience for this product.<br /> <br /> Make your artwork to inspire concepts, illustrate your imaginary world and/or highlight what's going on in the text. In games like Vampire and Exalted sexy is really not out of place, but you can titillate without objectifying. Also, assume the person holding the book can be woman, man, or anything in between, with an equally wide range of sexual preferences, and provide a power fantasy for all. <i>That</i> is your context nowadays, so embrace it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T05:59:14-07:00","id":1327397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327379#post1327379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Manufacturing humans for the express purpose of being objectified at best (leaving aside questions of a sufficiently different cultural background that it begs the question of what their impulse and standards for objectification are) is something a sorcerer might have conceivably done, but it's not the most pleasant thing to read about, and I wouldn't care for it being tossed in casually.<br /> <br /> I mean, presumably workings can be used to do a number of unpleasant things directly to people, but the examples overall seem to avoid that direction.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Things that might feel unduly unwelcoming to people who don't deserve it, for a start.<br /> <br /> The issue I would see is when it talks about <u>making</u> sexy people, especially when they're all women.<br /> </div> </div> </div>You went ant outright ignored my part where I say that particular case is easy to write off. You're not really answering what I said if you pick just the bits that you want for it.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> The world getting gradually better over time is not an insidious plot to catch people out, though.<br /> <br /> A person who is actually serious about the value of better social attitudes involved in representation is not somebody who should be upset by the notion that people in the future may see their attitudes and art as being quaint at best. </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what you are trying to say here. I posited that changes in the status quo aren't good or bad just because they are changes, and thus they should be evaluated. Artistic trends, in this particular case. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Minority voices in one's public deserve to be listened to when they bring up topics concerned with harmful language or representation.<br /> <br /> This should not harm one's majority audience, and of it does, one should question of that's an audience one should want. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say any particular person doesn't deserve to be listened to.<br /> <br /> I said it's impossible to please everyone, and this forces you to choose who will be heard.<br /> There's nothing wrong with this. In fact, your next line is in absolute agreement to my question: Pick your audience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T06:05:25-07:00","id":1327399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327380#post1327380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, and coming back to tabletop rpg's, if you want me to flip through your book and be inspired and fired up to make a character, good artwork for that would be a woman who is sexy as well as looks as if she has agency, motivation, personality, dignity and autonomy. You know, just like the male characters are supposed to be. The usual vacant-eyed, slack-jawed floozy, impossibly bent so both her breasts and ass are prominently visible, passively doing nothing, yeah, no, does nothing except making me wonder if I'm even the target audience for this product.</div> </div> </div> </div>The generic floozy doesn't particularly inspire me either. I, however, am admitting that it might inspire someone else. Clearly not you. Clearly not me. But you and I are not everyone, are we? This is the core of my point in this particular reply that you quoted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Make your artwork to inspire concepts, illustrate your imaginary world and/or highlight what's going on in the text. In games like Vampire and Exalted sexy is really not out of place, but you can titillate without objectifying. Also, assume the person holding the book can be woman, man, or anything in between, with an equally wide range of sexual preferences, and provide a power fantasy for all. <i>That</i> is your context nowadays, so embrace it. </div> </div> </div>I wholeheartedly agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T06:38:49-07:00","id":1327407,"title":"","content":"Also there is the age factor to figure in, since those of ages lower than 18 may be playing as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T07:14:17-07:00","id":1327414,"title":"","content":"Which is another very valid and more concrete question. Is Exalted for kids? It's clearly not PG-13, and as far as I care it shouldn't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T07:25:20-07:00","id":1327416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327414#post1327414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is another very valid and more concrete question. Is Exalted for kids? It's clearly not PG-13, and as far as I care it shouldn't be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that goes to play styles. While yes many things described in the setting are adult themed, like the Regent pleasuring himself all day, the group I play with tend to have stuff like that more in the background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T07:28:11-07:00","id":1327419,"title":"","content":"This is a question on how it's written, who it's intended to, not how each person plays it.<br /> <br /> I mean: If you write a setting with wars and murder, slavery, sex, drugs, tyrants and monsters, it's not a setting for kids, even if you manage to sanitize it into one when you play it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T07:59:21-07:00","id":1327424,"title":"","content":"To be fair, history has <i>all those things</i>, and we teach it to kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T08:27:32-07:00","id":1327430,"title":"","content":"Are they portrayed and depicted with the expectancy that the players can play into those subjects, or just cited? Is the educational context different from the entertainment context? Do we teach those to little kids? To teenagers?<br /> <br /> It's a rather touching difference, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Unless you want to make the argument that such content filter advisors are not important? It's probably too off-topic, but we can broach it somewhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 07-25-2019, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T08:39:12-07:00","id":1327435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327397#post1327397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You went ant outright ignored my part where I say that particular case is easy to write off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I was not really sure what you meant by it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand what you are trying to say here. I posited that changes in the status quo aren't good or bad just because they are changes, and thus they should be evaluated. Artistic trends, in this particular case.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did you mean by &quot;overton's a bitch&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say any particular person doesn't deserve to be listened to.<br /> <br /> I said it's impossible to please everyone, and this forces you to choose who will be heard.<br /> There's nothing wrong with this. In fact, your next line is in absolute agreement to my question: Pick your audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you said was questioning whether or not dissatisfied people constitute a loud minority who aren't representative of one's &quot;public&quot;.<br /> <br /> What you're saying now reads a lot different than your prior statement of &quot;you've got to be careful not to think the complainers are more representative than they are, lest you lose your public&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T08:43:28-07:00","id":1327437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327419#post1327419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a question on how it's written, who it's intended to, not how each person plays it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't play styles influence future writings though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T08:44:55-07:00","id":1327438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327430#post1327430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they portrayed and depicted with the expectancy that the players can play into those subjects, or just cited?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't play history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327430#post1327430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the educational context different from the entertainment context?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that Exalted has its moments of being educational (and of course history can be entertaining). My first memory of encountering the word &quot;satrapy&quot; was in the 2e core book, and it was through <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar229_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"229\" data-vbnamecard=\"229\">Stephen Lea Sheppard</a>'s posts that I came to learn that the notion of barter as I learned about it in school was largely a fanciful myth from a man who wanted to prove the existence of God.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327430#post1327430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we teach those to little kids? To teenagers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not as much as we should, honestly. America's really failing its future generations right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327430#post1327430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a rather touching difference, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>A not being B shouldn't always restrict it from being mentioned in a discussion on the subject of B, though. Especially in the case of a B that's so heavily informed by A.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327430#post1327430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you want to make the argument that such content filter advisors are not important?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not remotely what my argument is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-25-2019, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T09:19:52-07:00","id":1327447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327435#post1327435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did you mean by &quot;overton's a bitch&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>When we take something as the current norm, outliers are more salient. And when what we take as the norm changes, so do what is salient.<br /> When that change in the norm is good, all is good in the world.<br /> But when that change isn't, now something that could totally be fine now isn't.<br /> <br /> And realizing that the fact an element is an outlier has tangible weight in how we evaluate it isn't natural, it requires conscious effort. This is what I mean with &quot;Overton's a bitch&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you said was questioning whether or not dissatisfied people constitute a loud minority who aren't representative of one's &quot;public&quot;.<br /> <br /> What you're saying now reads a lot different than your prior statement of &quot;you've got to be careful not to think the complainers are more representative than they are, lest you lose your public&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I was at first focusing on the fact visibility is biased towards complainers, which has to be accounted if you don't want to misjudge. The latter statement is just a broader explanation of the same thing.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327437#post1327437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't play styles influence future writings though?</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Writers' play styles definitely influence how they write, but we were talking about the readers' play styles.<br /> The road from &quot;these readers like it like this&quot; to &quot;this is written like this&quot; has to first go through steps like &quot;this is selling well/badly&quot; and &quot;people are praising/complaining&quot;. From there you still have to make the writers change their style accordingly, or change the writers.<br /> <br /> Is this what you mean? If so, yeah, I agree.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327438#post1327438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't play history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, that's why I questioned the comparison: If we are concerned with who this book is suitable to, it has to be in the context of the game. Talking about something majorly different demands that difference to be acknowledged.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T02:43:01-07:00","id":1327551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1324617-women-in-armor-ii?p=1327399#post1327399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The generic floozy doesn't particularly inspire me either. I, however, am admitting that it might inspire someone else. Clearly not you. Clearly not me. But you and I are not everyone, are we? This is the core of my point in this particular reply that you quoted.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I was talking about an objectified and sexualized piece of artwork I am sure it will inspire <i>something </i>in someone. This has its purpose, obviously, and I've heard that, besides cat pics, it is one of the bigger raisons d'\u00eatre of the internet ;-) In a rpg manual it will also be off-putting to a growing number of people, however, and I dare say that, while you and me are indeed not everyone, those who find that type of art inspires actual <i>character concepts</i>, would also find non-objectified art to fulfill that function. <br /> <br /> Now, in addition to pushing away some people, I'm willing to go out on a limb again and state that the average consumer of rpg's does not <i>need </i>such artwork in their product and that even if some of them are incapable of distinguishing between sexy and sexualized, I would expect an art director to do so. I am not saying to let perfect be the enemy of good, and as you say, tastes and tolerances differ from person to person, so, yes, especially in properties in which sexy is the expected esthetic there will be hits and misses, depending on you who ask. That is ok.<br /> <br /> What is not ok is not making the effort if you want your work to appeal to a broader base. Especially as this is, you know, the 21th century. These days I can actually find rpg's, comics, computer games and all that where the makers at least try. My assumption is that not caring is effectively messaging to me, the consumer, who is your intended target-audience.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T05:32:32-07:00","id":1327559,"title":"","content":"I think also there's matter of numbers.<br /> <br /> If you have an RPG book with a picture of a sexualised passive woman (perhaps draped across the feet of a muscled barbarian king, in stereotypical fashion), I think that's okay... if there's 20 other pictures of active female badass heroines (and villainesses) doing stuff, and maybe some regular women just doing regular stuff (farming, shopkeeping, fishing, shepherdessing, etc).<br /> <br /> If there's 20 pictures of sexy girls reclining in a contorted position (to show both t and a), and only 1 badass heroine, it becomes the default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}